  "description": "DeepText Analyzer is a Python\u2011based project for analyzing large corpora of text with deep learning models. The code lives at https://github.com/example/deeptext-analyzer and the full documentation can be found at https://example.github.io/deeptext-analyzer/docs. It is tagged for \u201cnlp\u201d, \u201cdeep-learning\u201d, \u201ctext-analysis\u201d, and \u201cpython\u201d. To run on a cluster you should point the scheduler to the configuration file\u202fconf/cluster.yaml. The cluster resources can be tuned with two parameters: **num_nodes** (an integer, default\u202f2, allowed values\u202f1,\u202f2,\u202f4,\u202f8) and **gpu_type** (a string, default\u202f\u201cV100\u201d, choices\u202f\u201cV100\u201d,\u202f\u201cA100\u201d,\u202f\u201cK80\u201d). The execution environment is provided by the Docker image\u202fdocker.io/example/deeptext:latest; alternatively you can build it from the Dockerfile in the project root. Python dependencies are listed in requirements.txt, and after the container is ready you should run the setup shell commands `pip install -e .` followed by `python -m spacy download en_core_web_sm`.  \n\nThe project defines two main commands. The **train** command (`python train.py --epochs {epochs} --batch-size {batch_size}`) launches model training inside a tmux session. It accepts an **epochs** parameter (int, default\u202f10, choices\u202f5,\u202f10,\u202f20,\u202f50) and a **batch_size** parameter (int, default\u202f32, choices\u202f16,\u202f32,\u202f64,\u202f128). The **evaluate** command (`python evaluate.py --model-path {model_path}`) runs evaluation without tmux and takes a **model_path** string parameter, defaulting to\u202fmodels/latest.pt. After a run you can expect to find the artefacts\u202fmodels/latest.pt,\u202freports/metrics.json, and\u202flogs/train.log in the project directory."
